          %h2#TheSignRuleFromInternalization The sign rule from internalization
          %p
            Here and in the following we adopt the perpective that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+algebra"} homological algebra
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superalgebra"} superalgebra
            is concerned with the study of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+spaces"} super vector spaces
            (
            %a{:href => "#Deligne90"}> Deligne 90
            ) or equivalently internal to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpoints"} superpoints
            (
            %a{:href => "#Schwarz84"}> Schwarz 84
            ). This means that there are two contributions to the sign when exchanging two terms, one from the cohomological grading, one from the super-grading. This is “the sign rule” also used for instance in (
            %a{:href => "#CastellaniDAuriaFre91"}> Castellani-D’Auria-Fré 91, equation (II.2.106)
            ,
            %a{:href => "#BonoraBregolaLechnerPastiTonin87"} Bonora-Bregola-Lechner-Pasti-Tonin 87
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#DeligneFreed99"} Deligne-Freed 99, section 6
          %p
            There is however also a different sign rule use in the literature, the relation to which we discuss
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#SuperOddConvention"} below
          %h3#DifferentialFormsOnSupermanifolds Differential forms on supermanifolds
          %p
            We discuss the sign rules for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+algebra"} de Rham algebra
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superdifferential+forms"}> superdifferential forms
            ), which is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded-commutative+superalgebra"} differential graded-commutative superalgebra
          %p
            For
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p,q \in \mathbb{N}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{p|q}
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Cartesian+space"} super Cartesian space
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p|q)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
            defined by the fact that its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+functions"} algebra of functions
            is freely generated, as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+superalgebra"} smooth superalgebra
            by even-graded
            = succeed "-functions" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate"} coordinate
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
