          %h3#cohomology_of_super_minkowski_spacetime Cohomology of super Minkowski spacetime
          %p
            The above signs rules for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms+on+supermanifolds"} differential forms on supermanifolds
            directly translate to the signs rule for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+invariant+differential+forms"} left invariant differential forms
            on the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+group"} super Lie group
          %p
            We discuss now the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+translation+Lie+algebra"} super translation Lie algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} super Poincaré Lie algebra
            by the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentz+Lie+algebra"} Lorentz Lie algebra
          %p
            This is the sub-algebra of the
            %a{:href => "#DifferentialFormsOnSupermanifolds"} above
            de Rham complex of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+invariant+differential+forms"} left invariant differential forms
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ;
                      %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi li
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ;
                      %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ;
                      %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CE(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1;N})
                  \=
                  \\Omega^\bullet_{li}(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1;N})
                  \\hookrightarrow
                  \\Omega^\bullet(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1;N})
                  \\,.
          %p
            With the
            %a{:href => "#DifferentialFormsOnSupermanifolds"} above
            notation these are
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi α
                  %mo ≔
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %msup
                    %mi θ
                    %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\psi^\alpha \coloneqq \mathbf{d}\theta^\alpha
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mi a
                  %mo ≔
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi a
                  %mo +
                  %mover
                    %mi θ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %msup
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi a
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %mi θ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  e^a \coloneqq \mathbf{d}x^a + \bar{\theta} \Gamma^a \mathbf{d}\theta
                  \\,.
          %p
            With the
            %a{:href => "#DifferentialFormsOnSupermanifolds"} above
            sign rules it follows that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 2
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  e^{a_1} \wedge e^{a_2} = + e^{a_2} \wedge e^{a_1}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mi a
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi α
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi α
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  e^{a} \wedge \psi^\alpha = - \psi^\alpha \wedge e^a
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ψ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mn 1
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi ψ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %msup
                    %mi ψ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mn 2
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi ψ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\psi^{\alpha_1} \wedge \psi^{\alpha_2}
                  \=
                  +
                  \\psi^{\alpha_2} \wedge \psi^{\alpha_1}
                  \\,.
          %h3#super_lie_algebra_cohomology Super Lie algebra cohomology
          %p
            More generally, since the super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
            is identified with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+invariant+differential+forms"} left invariant differential forms
            on the corresponding
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+group"} super Lie group
            %a{:href => "#DifferentialFormsOnSupermanifolds"} above
            induce the cotresponding sign rule for the computation of super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"}> Lie algebra cohomology
            \.
          %h3#presheaves_on_superpoints Presheaves on superpoints
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Superpoint
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Superpoint
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpoints"} superpoints
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
            of that of real finitely-generated
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmann+algebras"} Grassmann algebras
          %p
            We list the terms with crucial signs that appear when regarding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superalgebra"} superalgebra
            as algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpoints"} superpoints
            (see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+infinity-groupoid"} super infinity-groupoid
            for background).
          %h4#super_lie_algebras Super Lie algebras
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpoint"} superpoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{0|q}
            write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕘
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mi even
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi Vect
                    %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{g}(\mathbb{R}^{0|q})
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\left(
                  \\mathfrak{g}\otimes C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^{0|q})
                  \\right)_{even}
                  \\in Vect_{\mathbb{R}}
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            which is the even-degree part of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            of the underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            and of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmann+algebra"} Grassmann algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^{0|q})
          %p
            Here if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{e_a, \psi_\alpha\}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis"} basis
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{e_a\}
            a basis for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mi even
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_{even}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\psi_\alpha\}
            a basis for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mi odd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_{odd}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mi i
                  %msubsup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\epsilon^i\}_{i = 1}^q
            for the generators of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^{0|q})
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕘
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{g}(\mathbb{R}^{0|q})
            is generated from elements of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi a
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi a
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 3
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 4
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ⋯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  e_a, \; e_a \epsilon^{i_1} \epsilon^{i_2},\;
                  e_a \epsilon^{i_1} \epsilon^{i_2} \epsilon^{i_3} \epsilon^{i_4}
                  ,\;
                  \\cdots
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi α
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi α
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 3
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\psi_\alpha \epsilon^{i_1} ,\;
                  \\psi_\alpha \epsilon^{i_1} \epsilon^{i_2} \epsilon^{i_3}
                  ,\;
                  \\cdots
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+bracket"} Lie bracket
            on the ordinary vector space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}(\mathbb{R}^{0|q})
            is defined on elements
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi κ
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mi even
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  x_i \kappa_i \in
                  \\left(
                  \\mathfrak{g}\otimes C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^{0|q})
                  \\right)_{even}
          %p by the formula
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi κ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi κ
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %msub
                    %mi κ
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi κ
                    %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [ x_1 \kappa_1 , x_2 \kappa_2]_{\mathfrak{g}(\mathbb{R}^{0|q})}
                  \\coloneqq
                  [x_1, x_2]_{\mathfrak{g}} \kappa_1 \kappa_2
                  \\,.
          %p Some examples:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [e_{a_1}, e_{a_2}]_{\mathfrak{g}(\mathbb{R}^{0|q})}
                  \=
                  [e_{a_1}, e_{a_2}]_{\mathfrak{g}}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi α
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi α
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [e_{a}, \psi_{\alpha} \epsilon^1]_{\mathfrak{g}(\mathbb{R}^{0|q})}
                  \=
                  [e_{a}, \psi_{\alpha}]_{\mathfrak{g}} \epsilon^1
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi α
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi α
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [\psi_{\alpha} \epsilon^1, e_a]_{\mathfrak{g}(\mathbb{R}^{0|q})}
                  \=
                  [\psi_{\alpha}, e_a]_{\mathfrak{g}} \epsilon^1
          %p
            From this and from the ordinary skew-symmetry of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+bracket"} Lie bracket
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}(\mathbb{R}^{0|q})
            follows that also in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
            we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi α
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [e_a, \psi_{\alpha}] = - [\psi_{\alpha}, e_a]_{\mathfrak{g}}
                  \\,.
          %p Next, from
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [\psi_{\alpha_1} \epsilon^1, \psi_{\alpha_2} \epsilon^2]_{\mathfrak{g}(\mathbb{R}^{0|q})}
                  \=
                  [\psi_{\alpha_1}, \psi_{\alpha_2}]_{\mathfrak{g}} \epsilon^1 \epsilon^2
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [\psi_{\alpha_2} \epsilon^2, \psi_{\alpha_1} \epsilon^1]_{\mathfrak{g}(\mathbb{R}^{0|q})}
                  \=
                  [\psi_{\alpha_2}, \psi_{\alpha_1}]_{\mathfrak{g}} \epsilon^2 \epsilon^1
          %p
            and the fact that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon^1  \epsilon^2 = - \epsilon^2  \epsilon^1
            it follows that in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [\psi_{\alpha_1}, \psi_{\alpha_2}]_{\mathfrak{g}}
                  \=
                  +
                  [\psi_{\alpha_2}, \psi_{\alpha_1}]_{\mathfrak{g}}
                  \\,.
          %h4#chevalleyeilenberg_algebra Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
