            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+spaces"} super vector spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded-commutative+superalgebras"} differential graded-commutative superalgebras
            are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid+objects"} commutative monoid objects
            with respect to these two choices.
          %p
            We now show that the two braidings are equivalent (Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EquivalenceTwoSymmetricMonoidalStructuresOnChSuperVect"}
            below), which immediately implies that the two categories of differential graded-commutative algebras are equivalent.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          #ChainComplexesOfSuperVectorSpaces.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+spaces"} super vector spaces
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi SuperVect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch(SuperVect)
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} category of chain complexes
              inside the category of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+spaces"} super vector spaces
            %p
              Hence for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi SuperVect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_\bullet \in Ch(SuperVect)
              an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{Z}
              there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+space"} super vector space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi even
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi odd
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi SuperVect
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    V_n = (V_n)_{even} \oplus (V_n)_{odd} \;\in SuperVect
            %p
              where we write the elements of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+order+two"} group of order two
              as
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi even
                      %mo ,
                      %mi odd
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2 =\{even, odd\}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi even
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} even
              being the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neutral+element"} neutral element
            %p
              Hence we may regard any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi SuperVect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_\bullet \in Ch(SuperVect)
              equivalently as a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo ×
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \times (\mathbb{Z}/2)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+object"} graded
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
              equipped with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
              of degree
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi even
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,even)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in V
              an element in definite (“homogeneous”) bi-degree, we denote this degree by
            #eq:BidegreeOnChainComplexOfSuperVectorSpaces.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi deg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mi v
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    deg(v) \coloneqq (n_v, \sigma_v) \;\in\; \mathbb{Z} \times (\mathbb{Z}/2)
                    \\,.
            %p
              The category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi SuperVect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch(SuperVect)
              becomes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
              under the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+chain+complexes"} tensor product of chain complexes
              applied to the tensor product of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+spaces"} super vector spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi W
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi SuperVect
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V, W \in Ch(SuperVect)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
              on a homogeneously graded element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi w
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \otimes w \in V \otimes W
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi w
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi w
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mi v
                    %mi v
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi w
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\partial(v \otimes w)
                    \\;=\;
                    (\partial v) \otimes w
                    +
                    (-1)^{ n_v } v \otimes \partial w
                    \\,.
          #SymmetricStructureOnCategoryOfChainComplexesOfSuperVectorSpaces.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
                on
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes+of+super+vector+spaces"} category of chain complexes of super vector spaces
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes+of+super+vector+spaces"} category of chain complexes of super vector spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi SuperVect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Ch(SuperVect), \otimes)
              from Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ChainComplexesOfSuperVectorSpaces"}
              becomes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal
              with each of the following two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braiding"} braiding
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:BidegreeOnChainComplexOfSuperVectorSpaces"} (1)
              as follows:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi Deligne
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi v
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi w
                        %mo ↦
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mi v
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mi w
                            %mo +
                            %msub
                              %mi σ
                              %mi v
                            %msub
                              %mi σ
                              %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi w
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi v
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_{Deligne} \;\colon\; v \otimes w \mapsto (-1)^{ (n_v n_w + \sigma_v \sigma_w) } w \otimes v
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi Bernst
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi v
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi w
                        %mo ↦
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mi v
                            %mo +
                            %msub
                              %mi σ
                              %mi v
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mi w
                            %mo +
                            %msub
                              %mi σ
                              %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi w
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi v
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_{Bernst} \;\colon\; v \otimes w \mapsto (-1)^{ (n_v + \sigma_v) (n_w + \sigma_w) } w \otimes v
                  \.
            %p
              Here in the exponents we are using the canonical
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              and on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+field"} prime field
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝔽
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2 = \mathbb{F}_2
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+homomorphism"} ring homomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{Z}/2
              and we understand that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi even
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1)^{even} = 1
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi odd
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1)^{odd} = -1
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Since the expressions for both sign factors are symmetric in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
              in both cases, it is clear that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mrow
                        %mi w
                        %mo ,
                        %mi v
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ,
                        %mi w
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_{w,v} \circ \tau_{v,w} = id_{v \otimes w}
              in both cases. Hence if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi τ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
              is indeed a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braiding"} braiding
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric
            %p
              To see that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi τ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
              is indeed a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braiding"} braiding
              in each case, we need to check the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hexagon+identities"} hexagon identities
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
